  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1245 AM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nUpper level ridge across the Southeast will continue to dominate\nthe weather pattern across Texas into the July 4th weekend. Hot\nconditions will prevail with temperatures near or above 100 across\nmuch of the area. Should see some decrease in the surface pressure\ngradient so wind speeds should at least decrease for the 4th.\n\nBit of a pattern change will take place early next week, as the\nridge weakens to the east and a second ridge tries to develop \nover the western US. This sets up an upper level shear axis across\nthe Southern Plains, with a weak upper low eventually developing \nin its base across Texas. Models have started to pick up on this \nand model blends have increased rain chances for Sunday and \nMonday. System is still forecasted to be weak so not expecting \nanything widespread, but after a stretch of no rain at all, even \nsome scattered convection and a little cooler temperatures will be\nwelcome.",
